.TH geectl-build-buildconfig 1  "geectl-build-buildconfig 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-build\-buildconfig \- Read the build configuration for a project/repository: the expanded `_buildconfig` text the engine takes as `\-\-dist`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl build buildconfig\fR [\fB\-\-alternative\-project\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIREPOSITORY\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read the build configuration for a project/repository: the expanded `_buildconfig` text the engine takes as `\-\-dist`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-alternative\-project\fR \fI<ALTERNATIVE_PROJECT>\fR
Read the build configuration for another project instead of `project`: the expanded `_buildconfig` text the engine takes as `\-\-dist` there
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project to read the build configuration for
.TP
<\fIREPOSITORY\fR>
The repository to read the build configuration for
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
